# macOS and iCloud artefacts.
#
# This repository currently lives under an iCloud-synchronised Desktop path,
# and iCloud resolves sync conflicts by writing a second copy beside the
# original: "china 2.json", "index 2.html", "bd-registry-types 2.cjs". A single
# session produced 72 of them. They are not source, they break the registry
# loader's orphan-file guard, and one careless `git add -A` would commit them.
#
# Two saved HTTP responses did reach a release this way and had to be removed
# afterwards, so this file exists to make that failure impossible rather than
# merely unlikely.
.DS_Store
._*
*.icloud
Icon?

# iCloud conflict copies: "name 2.ext", "name 3.ext", and the bare form.
* [0-9].*
* [0-9]
*conflicted copy*
* copy.*
* copy

# Merge and editor debris.
*.orig
*.rej
*~
.*.swp

# Dependencies and local environment.
node_modules/
.env
.env.*

# Tender opportunity ingestion cache.
#
# scripts/ingest-tender-opportunities.cjs writes one snapshot per source under
# data/tender-opportunities/snapshots/. Those are the RAW normalized records —
# 43 MB across five sources, rewritten on every refresh — and committing them
# would add tens of megabytes of history per ingestion run for data that is
# already carried, deduplicated, in opportunities.json.
#
# The corpus IS committed: it is what the site build reads, and the build must
# work from git alone with no network. The snapshots are a local cache that
# ingestion rebuilds by fetching. See docs/TENDER-OPPORTUNITY-INTELLIGENCE-V1.md
# for what this costs (the collapse guard falls back to the committed corpus's
# per-source counts on a fresh clone) and why it is the right trade for v1.
data/tender-opportunities/snapshots/
